From 1a781d4214405a9932eccdaba7ff13c55aa656b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:08:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Respawn guard: release active_pr once for a
 re-review linked after the owner's checkpoint that approves the current PR
 head

Card t_01a1cde626be2ada (PR #1223) stayed respawn_guarded active_pr after re-review
t_01a1ce6ea64f8fce approved the exact head: the owner's only review_checkpoint named the
old review A, and the orchestrator added B with kanban_link, which is not an owner park.
resumes_review required the parent set to equal the checkpoint's, so B could never count.

A parent absent from the checkpoint now counts as awaited when every linked/unlinked event
for it on the owner's card is strictly after the park, it completed (claimed, after the
park) with verdict approve or a change request, it names a checkpointed PR via
pr/reviewed_pr, and its reviewed_sha equals that PR's current GitHub headRefOid (gh,
cached 60 s). It then joins the named-awaited union. Every other resumes_review check is
unchanged, the next claim consumes the continuation, and unreadable provenance or an
unknown head keeps the hold.

Task: t_01a1cea62abc507b
